  "final_span": "military's \"certified\" launchers capable of going from pad ready to space worthy in as few as 50 days, not counting time-pressure mandated delays. In June, SpaceX secured another historic first by winning a contract through the American Civilian Services Administration -- the public services arm of the government's \"go to\" government solutions -- as the official Civilian Launch Provider, once again outpacing both Orbital ATK and Boeing in the competition.\nIt would have been an unrivaled streak, were it possible to maintain it unbeaten, given SpaceX's previous assertion that timing for launch is the sole criterion in a competitive business focused on success. But podium positions are still podium positions, and this time SpaceX outshined all expectations by being the fastest-growing participant.\nSo now Musk and his team will have the extra time needed to figure out how a missile",
